course: dictionary
lesson: 6839
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it. The word outing is a good example. It can mean a short trip out for fun, a walk out of the house, or a game played by a team.
explain: Look at the context. «Rat and Mole were coming back after a long day's outing with Otter, hunting and exploring on the wide uplands.» They have been out all day with a friend, having fun and exploring, so outing means a trip out for fun.
explain: Other clue words help too. Words like class, team or family tell you which meaning fits. A class outing is a trip away from school. A team's outing is one game or race. Always ask: which meaning makes sense in this sentence?
fact: Outing means a short trip out for fun, often with a group.
fact: A class outing is a trip to a zoo, a museum or somewhere else away from school.
fact: In sport, an outing is one appearance by a player or team in a game or race.
fact: Outing can also mean telling everyone a secret about someone without their permission, which is unkind and can hurt.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Rat and Mole came back after a long day's outing with Otter.» What is the outing here? | A school test | A secret told to everyone | *A trip out for fun | A sports game
exercise: «Mia's first outing for the team ended in a win.» What does outing mean here? | Her first trip to the shops | A walk around the park | A secret told about her | *Her first game for the team
exercise: Priya told the whole class who Sam liked, without asking him first. What is this called? | A class trip to the museum | *An outing that is unkind, telling a secret without permission | An outing that is unkind | A family day out
test: Dad said, «Let's go on a family outing to the park.» What does outing mean? | A test at school | *A short trip out for fun | A secret about someone | A team game
test: The class went on a ___ to the zoo. Which word fits best? | ladder | bundle | *outing | hunger
exam: «Her first outing for the team was a win.» Which meaning is right? | Her first walk in the park | Her first trip to the shops | Her first secret told to a friend | *Her first game or race for the team
